IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wrca-dates`
IMPORT `wrca-core`
IMPORT `wrca-seat`
IMPORT `wrca-seat-employer`

-- Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 (Tas) -- cases for the employer's seat (wrca-seat-employer.l4), with
-- mirror cases against the worker's seat (wrca-seat.l4): the same facts asked from both seats must give the same answer.
--
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from the deposited text, with the arithmetic in the comment above the
-- assertion. Mia's employer, a Hobart warehouse company insured with a licensed insurer and working Monday to Friday,
-- learns of her back injury on Monday 2 March 2026 and receives her claim on Wednesday 11 March 2026. Her first pay day
-- after the claim is Thursday 19 March.

§ `Am I liable to compensate this worker?`

#ASSERT `Am I liable to compensate this worker` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the employer is liable to pay compensation (s 25(1))`
-- A disease to which the work was not the major or most significant factor: not liable.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to compensate this worker` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not liable: the employment was not the major or most significant factor in the disease (s 25(1)(b), s 3(2A))`
-- Mirror: the same facts from both seats.
#ASSERT `Am I liable to compensate this worker` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Is my employer liable to compensate me for this injury` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I liable to compensate this worker` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Is my employer liable to compensate me for this injury` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I liable to compensate this worker` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Is my employer liable to compensate me for this injury` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE

§ `What must I do on a claim, and by when?`

-- s 33A: told on 2 March: the notice by 16 March. Told by the claim: no notice needed. Mirror.
#ASSERT `By when must I tell this worker of the right to claim` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `the employer must inform the worker of the right to claim, in the Schedule 1 form, on or before` (`the calendar date` 16 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I tell this worker of the right to claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `no notice is needed: the employer was informed of the injury by the service of a claim (s 33A(2))`
#ASSERT `By when must I tell this worker of the right to claim` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `By when must my employer tell me of my right to claim` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE
-- s 36(1AA): 3 working days after Wednesday 11 March: Thu 12, Fri 13, Mon 16, so by Monday 16 March. With one closure
-- day in that week, Tuesday 17 March. A self-insurer: not applicable.
#ASSERT `By when must I notify my insurer of this claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) TRUE `Monday to Friday` 0 EQUALS `on or before` (`the calendar date` 16 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I notify my insurer of this claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) TRUE `Monday to Friday` 1 EQUALS `on or before` (`the calendar date` 17 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I notify my insurer of this claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) FALSE `Monday to Friday` 0 EQUALS `not applicable: the employer has no licensed insurer`
-- s 36(1)(b): 5 working days: Thu 12, Fri 13, Mon 16, Tue 17, Wed 18, so by Wednesday 18 March. At a seven-day site:
-- Thu 12 to Mon 16, so by Monday 16 March.
#ASSERT `By when must I forward the claim to my insurer` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) TRUE `Monday to Friday` 0 EQUALS `on or before` (`the calendar date` 18 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I forward the claim to my insurer` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) TRUE `every day of the week` 0 EQUALS `on or before` (`the calendar date` 16 3 2026)
-- s 39: by 8 April 2026. Mirror.
#ASSERT `By when must I tell the worker the status of the claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 8 4 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I tell the worker the status of the claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) EQUALS `By when must I be told whether my claim is accepted` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026)
-- s 81: first pay day 19 March, practicable: 19 March; not practicable: 25 March. A first pay day of 27 March (16 days
-- on): 27 March. Mirrors.
#ASSERT `By when must I start weekly payments` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `the calendar date` 19 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I start weekly payments` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `the calendar date` 25 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I start weekly payments` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 27 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `the calendar date` 27 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I start weekly payments` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `By when must my weekly payments start` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026) FALSE
#ASSERT `By when must I start weekly payments` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 27 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS `By when must my weekly payments start` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 27 3 2026) TRUE
-- s 81(3): from 2 March. A claim given on 1 June 2026 for an incapacity from 2 March: from 18 May 2026. Mirror.
#ASSERT `From what date must I pay weekly payments` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 2 3 2026
#ASSERT `From what date must I pay weekly payments` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 18 5 2026
#ASSERT `From what date must I pay weekly payments` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `From what date are my weekly payments payable` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026)
-- s 81A: by 3 June 2026 (84 days). s 81AB: disputed properly on 2 June: disputed; nothing done by 4 June: taken to have
-- accepted; on 1 May: still open until 3 June. Mirrors.
#ASSERT `By when must I dispute liability` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 3 6 2026
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have accepted liability for this claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 2 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 4 6 2026) EQUALS `liability is disputed in accordance with s 81A`
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have accepted liability for this claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 4 6 2026) EQUALS `liability is taken to have been accepted (s 81AB)`
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have accepted liability for this claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 2 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 4 6 2026) EQUALS `Is my employer taken to have accepted liability for my claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 2 6 2026) (`the calendar date` 4 6 2026)
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have accepted liability for this claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `Is my employer taken to have accepted liability for my claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 5 2026)

§ `Have I met my duties on this claim? Is a missed deadline a breach?`

-- On Friday 20 March 2026: the right-to-claim notice given 10 March (due 16 March): met. The insurer notified only on
-- Thursday 19 March (due Monday 16 March): missed, a breach. The claim forwarded 18 March (due 18 March): met. No status
-- notice yet (due 8 April): open. Weekly payments started 19 March (due 19 March): met.
`Mia's employer on 20 March` MEANS `Have I met my duties on this claim` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) TRUE `Monday to Friday` 0 (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 18 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 20 3 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 20 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Mia's employer on 20 March`'s `telling the worker of the right to claim (s 33A)` EQUALS `met`
#ASSERT `Mia's employer on 20 March`'s `notifying my insurer (s 36(1AA))` EQUALS `missed: a breach of the Act`
#ASSERT `Mia's employer on 20 March`'s `forwarding the claim to my insurer (s 36(1)(b))` EQUALS `met`
#ASSERT `Mia's employer on 20 March`'s `notifying the status of the claim (s 39)` EQUALS `still open, on or before` (`the calendar date` 8 4 2026)
#ASSERT `Mia's employer on 20 March`'s `starting weekly payments (s 81)` EQUALS `met`
-- On 10 April, still no status notice: missed, a breach of s 39.
#ASSERT (`Have I met my duties on this claim` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) TRUE `Monday to Friday` 0 (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 18 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 10 4 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 10 4 2026))'s `notifying the status of the claim (s 39)` EQUALS `missed: a breach of the Act`
-- A self-insurer, told of the injury by the claim, on a claim for expenses only: the s 33A, s 36 and s 81 duties are not
-- required; the s 39 notice given 1 April: met.
`a self-insurer's expenses claim` MEANS `Have I met my duties on this claim` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) FALSE `Monday to Friday` 0 (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 4 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 10 4 2026)
#ASSERT `a self-insurer's expenses claim`'s `telling the worker of the right to claim (s 33A)` EQUALS `not required`
#ASSERT `a self-insurer's expenses claim`'s `notifying my insurer (s 36(1AA))` EQUALS `not required`
#ASSERT `a self-insurer's expenses claim`'s `forwarding the claim to my insurer (s 36(1)(b))` EQUALS `not required`
#ASSERT `a self-insurer's expenses claim`'s `notifying the status of the claim (s 39)` EQUALS `met`
#ASSERT `a self-insurer's expenses claim`'s `starting weekly payments (s 81)` EQUALS `not required`

-- The same story as a regulative trace (wrca-core.l4), day 0 Wednesday 11 March 2026: insurer notified day 8 (19 March,
-- due day 5), claim forwarded day 7, payments started day 8, status notice day 20.
`Mia's employer's spans` MEANS `Claim duty spans` WITH
    `calendar days to the last day to notify the insurer`         IS 5
    `calendar days to the last day to forward the claim`          IS 7
    `calendar days to the last day to commence weekly payments`   IS 8
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 36(1AA): the employer must notify its insurer of the claim within 3 working days ..."
#TRACE `ss 36, 39, 81 -- the employer's duties on receiving a claim` TRUE TRUE `Mia's employer's spans` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `forward the completed claim and a copy to the licensed insurer` AT 7
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `notify the insurer of the claim` AT 8
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `commence weekly payments` AT 8
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `notify the worker in writing of the decision on liability, or why none has been made` AT 20
-- Had the insurer been notified on day 5 (Monday 16 March), every duty would have been met.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 36, 39, 81 -- the employer's duties on receiving a claim` TRUE TRUE `Mia's employer's spans`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `notify the insurer of the claim` 5), (EVENT `the employer` `forward the completed claim and a copy to the licensed insurer` 7), (EVENT `the employer` `commence weekly payments` 8), (EVENT `the employer` `notify the worker in writing of the decision on liability, or why none has been made` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 36(4): notified on 19 March, the insurer need not indemnify the weekly payments for 17 to 19 March. On 16 March: no gap.
#ASSERT `For which days does my insurer not indemnify me` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026) TRUE `Monday to Friday` 0 EQUALS `the insurer need not indemnify the weekly payments for the days` (`the calendar date` 17 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 19 3 2026)
#ASSERT `For which days does my insurer not indemnify me` (`the calendar date` 11 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 16 3 2026) TRUE `Monday to Friday` 0 EQUALS `no gap: the insurer was notified within the 3 working days`
-- Fines: weekly payments started 4 days late, 20 + 4 x 5 = 40 penalty units at most; refusing a claim, 50; infringement
-- notice for a late s 81 start by a company, 5; s 36(3) has none.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `not commencing weekly payments as s 81(1) requires (s 81(2))` 4 EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `refusing to receive a claim, hindering a claim, or dismissing a worker for claiming (s 36(3))` 0 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `What infringement notice penalty applies` `not commencing weekly payments as s 81(1) requires (s 81(2))` TRUE EQUALS `an infringement notice penalty, in penalty units, of` 5
#ASSERT `What infringement notice penalty applies` `refusing to receive a claim, hindering a claim, or dismissing a worker for claiming (s 36(3))` TRUE EQUALS `not an infringement notice offence (reg 28, Schedule 2)`

§ `How much must I pay this worker?`

-- Mia's normal weekly earnings: (80,000 - 4,000 - 2,000 - 5,000 + 4,000) / (365 / 7) = 1,400. Mirror.
#ASSERT `What are this worker's normal weekly earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2020) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) 80000 4000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2000 5000 FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0 30 40 EQUALS 1400
#ASSERT `What are this worker's normal weekly earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2020) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) 80000 4000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2000 5000 FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0 30 40 EQUALS `What are my normal weekly earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2020) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) 80000 4000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2000 5000 FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0 30 40
-- A second job of 300 a week, neither full-time: 1,700. Mirror.
#ASSERT `What are this worker's normal weekly earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2020) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) 80000 4000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2000 5000 TRUE 300 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0 30 40 EQUALS 1700
#ASSERT `What are this worker's normal weekly earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2020) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) 80000 4000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2000 5000 TRUE 300 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0 30 40 EQUALS `What are my normal weekly earnings` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2020) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) 80000 4000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 2000 5000 TRUE 300 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0 30 40
-- A new hire of 7 days with no comparable worker: 30 an hour x 40 hours = 1,200.
#ASSERT `What are this worker's normal weekly earnings` (`the calendar date` 23 2 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) 9000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 `none of the contracts is full-time` FALSE 0 30 40 EQUALS 1200
-- Weekly payment: total incapacity, 1,400; partial, earning 500 on suitable duties, 900. Mirrors.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay this worker each week before any step-down` 1400 TRUE TRUE 32 38 0 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1400
#ASSERT `How much must I pay this worker each week before any step-down` 1400 TRUE FALSE 32 38 0 500 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 900
#ASSERT `How much must I pay this worker each week before any step-down` 1400 TRUE FALSE 32 38 0 500 EQUALS `What is my weekly payment before any step-down` 1400 TRUE FALSE 32 38 0 500
#ASSERT `How much must I pay this worker each week before any step-down` 1400 FALSE TRUE 32 38 0 0 EQUALS `What is my weekly payment before any step-down` 1400 FALSE TRUE 32 38 0 0
-- Until when: Mia, not assessed, 2 March 2035; assessed at 17%, 12 years, 2 March 2038. Mirrors.
#ASSERT `Until when must I pay weekly payments` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0 EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2035) `9 years after the initial incapacity (s 69B(1)(c)(i), (2E)(a))`
#ASSERT `Until when must I pay weekly payments` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE 17 EQUALS `the entitlement to weekly payments ceases on` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2038) `12 years after the initial incapacity (s 69B(1)(c)(ii), (2E)(b))`
#ASSERT `Until when must I pay weekly payments` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE 17 EQUALS `When does my entitlement to weekly payments stop` (`the calendar date` 15 6 1990) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) TRUE 17
#ASSERT `Until when must I pay weekly payments` (`the calendar date` 10 8 1960) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0 EQUALS `When does my entitlement to weekly payments stop` (`the calendar date` 10 8 1960) 67 (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) FALSE 0
